The spectrum of the compact source was extracted from a circular region 2 pixels (0.984\\arcsec) in radius. The main source of background comes from thermal emission emitted by the gaseous remnant itself, which accounts for half the extracted counts (\\sim100 out of 193 total). Our spectral fit for the compact star, therefore, included a NEI thermal component with variable intensity, but fixed abundance (0.3 times solar), temperature and ionization timescale. The latter two quantities were determined by a spectral fit to data extracted from an annulus surrounding the point source covering 4-6 pixels in radius. Emission from the compact star was assumed to be either a blackbody or a power-law. Absorption, including Galactic and LMC components, was included as above. Table 2 shows the

